    "rationale": "absl::int128 / absl::uint128 are concrete 128-bit integer value types \u2014 an ideal real-library dunder-mapping target. The binder maps their member + free arithmetic/bitwise/comparison operators to Python dunders (__add__/__sub__/__mul__/__truediv__/__mod__/__and__/__or__/__xor__/__lshift__/__rshift__ + in-place, __eq__/__lt__/...), constructors from built-in integers, and __bool__/__int__/__float__ conversions. Their free operator<<(std::ostream&, ...) is surfaced as Python str() via __str__ (BINDER-0007 fix), used here as the differential oracle's value channel (128-bit results exceed Python-constructible range). Differentially checked vs native Abseil.",
